<section id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">In-Context Library</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our in-context library is a curated collection of code snippets that have demonstrated at least a 10% improvement in CLIP-alignment metrics when modifying a 3D environment. These snippets serve as in-context examples during generation. By randomly sampling from this library when producing candidate actions, the policy is nudged toward more diverse and effective action codes. After each self-improvement training round, newly discovered high-quality prompt and action code pairs are appended to this library. Below, we showcase an example code snippet from our in-context library for the prompt: <span id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">a chic hair salon with round mirrors, pink chairs, and pot plants</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="programs/in˙context.txt">⬇</a></div>
